        type: "p",
        text: "Frida Kahlo was breastfed by her mother only briefly, since her sister Cristina (the same sister with whom Frida's husband, the painter Diego Rivera, had a passionate affair that became public knowledge) was only eleven months younger than her. An Indigenous wet nurse was hired to breastfeed Frida, with whom the child did not have a harmonious relationship: the nurse did not love the little girl, and was not loved by her in return. One might therefore think that, if Frida's physical suffering began at six, when she fell ill with polio, her emotional suffering tied to loneliness began much earlier.",
