        type: "p",
        text: "The painting, like almost all of Frida's small-format works (30.5×34.7 cm), shows in the foreground the little girl suckling milk from one of the breasts of the nurse holding her in her arms. The nurse is monumental, bare-chested, her face concealed by a mask resembling the funerary attributes of Mexico's Indigenous peoples, which also hides her eyes. The visible lower part of her body is greyish in color, like rock. Frida has her adult face, with the typical thick black eyebrows and a slight dark down above her upper lip: her face is dissonant with her small body. No sign of emotional connection between the two figures emerges.",
